[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677281654","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-2677281654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":2677281654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6flBN2","user":{"login":"gokiburikin","id":3820082,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MjAwODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3820082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin","html_url":"https://github.com/gokiburikin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gokiburikin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T01:49:02Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T01:49:20Z","body":"The default callback modifier seems to be `Idle` which results in using the process delta not the physics delta. Does changing this setting to `Physics` on the skeleton solve the problem?\n\n[The line in question.](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0e3dbba6a58bc0f9b0d37b2d942d67cf7fcc49a5/scene/3d/spring_bone_simulator_3d.cpp#L1483)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677281654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677290528","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-2677290528","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":2677290528,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6flDYg","user":{"login":"Kekitopu","id":174217669,"node_id":"U_kgDOCmJZxQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174217669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu","html_url":"https://github.com/Kekitopu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T02:00:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T02:01:58Z","body":"> The default callback modifier seems to be `Idle` which results in using the process delta not the physics delta. Does changing this setting to `Physics` on the skeleton solve the problem?\n> \n> [The line in question.](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0e3dbba6a58bc0f9b0d37b2d942d67cf7fcc49a5/scene/3d/spring_bone_simulator_3d.cpp#L1483)\n\nno, it made the bone behave different but there are still diferences with framerate unlocked and locked with vsync","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677290528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677302741","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-2677302741","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":2677302741,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6flGXV","user":{"login":"Kekitopu","id":174217669,"node_id":"U_kgDOCmJZxQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174217669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu","html_url":"https://github.com/Kekitopu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T02:15:18Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T02:15:18Z","body":"Callback modifier is set to physics in this video.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/SVunDt78P0A\n\nits basically the same, movement increases as framerate goes down","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2677302741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692606379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-2692606379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":2692606379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gfemr","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-02T07:47:32Z","updated_at":"2025-03-02T14:43:43Z","body":"I'll see if I can find a better way to interpolate when I have time, but I suspect it is mostly a SpringBone specification (so if it can be solved, it will be provided as an option).\n\nFirst SpringBone translates joint and then converts it to a rotation by pushing out in the normal direction from center.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89da5bbe-8d9d-48d2-a43c-664c5921ed12)\n\nAs you can see in the figure above, at this point, the smaller the frame rate, the larger the velocity.\n\nSpringBone's algorithm calculates the next coordinate by integrating the velocity, so this difference affects the result. I marginally expect that the difference possibly be reduced by some approaches:\n\n1. Multiplying by some of the coefficients such as dependent on the pushing out distance, like some kind of averaging\n2. Predicts the next coordinate of the joint when there is no length limit based on velocity and calculates the pushing out point by including the predicted point as a factor in the calculation\n3. Pushing out a joint to a vector that is not from center. For example, create a plane ABC passing through three points: point A before the move, current point B, and center point C. In plane ABC, create a vector orthogonal to line AB and going from point B to the face of the sphere. two vectors are possible, the shorter of which is adopted. For example, in the figure above, we can consider a vector from t1 to up\n\nAlso, the other workaround I can think of is to simulate a lower frame rate in the `_process()` or `_physics_process()`, but I think we need to discuss whether it is good for Godot as a whole to manage FPS on a per-node basis. Perhaps the concept needs to be common for things like LOD of animation FPS.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2692606379/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974658010","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-2974658010","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":2974658010,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xTa3a","user":{"login":"squashiv","id":33762217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNzYyMjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33762217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv","html_url":"https://github.com/squashiv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/squashiv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-15T19:38:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T19:38:44Z","body":"Also worth a mention, physics interpolation doesn't affect SpringBoneSimulator3D i believe. Result of SpringBoneSimulator3D becomes jittery when used with physics interpolation enabled, or at least the result is not interpolated so the jittering becomes apparent.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2974658010/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3014039683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-3014039683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":3014039683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6zppiD","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-27T18:34:08Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T18:34:08Z","body":"> Also worth a mention, physics interpolation doesn't affect SpringBoneSimulator3D i believe. Result of SpringBoneSimulator3D becomes jittery when used with physics interpolation enabled, or at least the result is not interpolated so the jittering becomes apparent.\n\nSee https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10770.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3014039683/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403714132","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-3403714132","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":3403714132,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K4I5U","user":{"login":"apples","id":2352020,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTIwMjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2352020?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples","html_url":"https://github.com/apples","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apples/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T21:41:23Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T21:41:23Z","body":"I tested the MRP in 4.5 and latest master ([`0400b70`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/0400b703e4c95e7de0ee98688267b98a5fb5e358)).\n\nThe issue is still present when the skeleton's callback mode is Idle. Setting the skeleton's callback mode to Physics fixes the issue for me, although the lack of physics interpolation is noticeable.\n\nI feel like the best way to fix this issue would be to resolve the lack of physics interpolation. It might also be nice to be able to set the callback mode on each modifier rather than only on the whole skeleton.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403714132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403823562","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-3403823562","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":3403823562,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7K4jnK","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T22:31:07Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T22:50:40Z","body":"@apples Physical interpolation for node movement has been definitely added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110987.\n\nHowever, physical interpolation is not applied to the internal joint movement itself by SpringBone but since we are not using PhysicalServer for bone movement and it relies on integration math, it is unclear whether this can adopt physical interpolation.\n\nAlso if applying physical interpolation to SpringBone bones, I assume it should be implemented within the pose calculation in the Skeleton3D class and retrieved by a function like `get_bone_pose_interpolated()`.\n\nA concern is that parent bone movements may occur within the same frame as retrieving `get_bone_pose_interpolated()`. Therefore, it is unclear whether implementing this is technically feasible.\n\n@lawnjelly Do you have any ideas about incorporating something like physical interpolation into Skeleton3D's pose calculation?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3403823562/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3470651588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-3470651588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":3470651588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7O3fDE","user":{"login":"Kekitopu","id":174217669,"node_id":"U_kgDOCmJZxQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/174217669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu","html_url":"https://github.com/Kekitopu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kekitopu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-30T23:05:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-30T23:05:12Z","body":"> I tested the MRP in 4.5 and latest master ([`0400b70`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/0400b703e4c95e7de0ee98688267b98a5fb5e358)).\n> \n> The issue is still present when the skeleton's callback mode is Idle. Setting the skeleton's callback mode to Physics fixes the issue for me, although the lack of physics interpolation is noticeable.\n> \n> I feel like the best way to fix this issue would be to resolve the lack of physics interpolation. It might also be nice to be able to set the callback mode on each modifier rather than only on the whole skeleton.\n\nyeah setting it to physics makes it consistent but the lack of interpolation is really noticable if you have a high refresh rate monitor or if your physics ticks per second are set to something like 30","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3470651588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4704105399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-4704105399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":4704105399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGGLztw","user":{"login":"Midrule","id":59895191,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk1MTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59895191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule","html_url":"https://github.com/Midrule","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-15T02:59:52Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T02:59:52Z","body":"This issue makes SpringBoneSimulator3D a little unusable at the moment. It's either cap it at physics tick which behaves perfectly fine but it will visually be locked at physics (60), or look smooth at any framerate but completely freak out the higher the fps is","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4704105399/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497420947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5497420947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":5497420947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR6v8kw","user":{"login":"ImTiredRat","id":34012814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDEyODE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34012814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat","html_url":"https://github.com/ImTiredRat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T16:54:38Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T16:54:38Z","body":"I found that capping framerate at multiples of 60 (eg. at 30, 60, etc.) results in the spring bone acting as expecting, however if the FPS isn't a multple of 60, then the spring bone has issues and tends to act abnormally and over-step its springy-ness.\n[example videos on my reddit post](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1w40nc9/comment/p765irp/?screen_view_count=2&ext-referrer=DIRECT)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497420947/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497509078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5497509078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":5497509078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR61U1g","user":{"login":"Midrule","id":59895191,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5ODk1MTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59895191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule","html_url":"https://github.com/Midrule","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Midrule/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T17:01:42Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T17:01:42Z","body":"Interesting discovery. My monitor is 75hz so that would make sense why it’s acting really odd when running with vsync on that one","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497509078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5505032526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5505032526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":5505032526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSCAhTg","user":{"login":"ImTiredRat","id":34012814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDEyODE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34012814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat","html_url":"https://github.com/ImTiredRat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-02T05:44:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T05:44:02Z","body":"I dug through the c++ code and the culprit may be that it's using `get_global_transform_interpolated()` rather than just getting the transform directly? it's hard to piece it fully together but from my understanding the official documentation of this function states:\n\"`This is particularly important for frame-based operations that take place in Node._process()`\" which would be why it seems to be frame-dependent. there's no change if you're using Skeleton3D physics callback or idle callback either, so no matter which you use, it's tied to the framerate.\n\nI noticed this when I swapped my skeleton3D to physics callback, it would update on physics ticks but would still have the frame-dependent glitch of the lower the fps the more it 'glitches out'.\n\nI'm not 100% on my findings but this seems like the likely cause.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5505032526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5509221167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5509221167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":5509221167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSGALLw","user":{"login":"ImTiredRat","id":34012814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDEyODE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34012814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat","html_url":"https://github.com/ImTiredRat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-02T12:03:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T12:09:28Z","body":"can confirm, set center_from to an empty node, which means it pulls from an empty `Transform3D` rather than `global_transform_interpolated`\n\n<img width=\"233\" height=\"86\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5901764-5b1c-4dc8-ae94-d639c274d268\" />\n\nthen applied the player velocity via external_force\n\n<img width=\"598\" height=\"80\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1bf01d08-afe5-40a6-b81d-cdb6060dcdc5\" />\n\nand now it's entirely frame independant. I tested with 60fps, capped at 48fps and then 32fps and all three worked as expected.\n\nEDIT: downside to using this workaround, though, is you don't get the angular changes effecting the `SpringBoneSimulator3D`. eg. this gif:\n\n<img width=\"239\" height=\"201\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7f5c626-ff22-4ff7-8715-f04aefe70df9\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5509221167/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5510431152","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5510431152","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103229","id":5510431152,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSHKBsA","user":{"login":"ImTiredRat","id":34012814,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDEyODE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34012814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat","html_url":"https://github.com/ImTiredRat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImTiredRat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-02T13:38:04Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T20:30:50Z","body":"so.. I compiled Godot 4.7.2.stable with the single change of changing those two lines from `get_global_transform_interpolated()` to `get_global_transform()` and.. it didn't seem to change anything.\n\nsetting skeleton callback mode to physics seems to do the trick, at least in 4.7.2. experimented a bit and the issue weirdly was the bone drag variable. setting it to 1.0 (disabling drag all together) removes the 'wild flailing' that you see with the bone. high velocity creates high drag which creates wild flailing bones.\n\nhere's drag at 0.0:\n<img width=\"391\" height=\"386\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a14663fc-fb17-4a34-a026-db360c7cdbd6\" />\n\nand here's drag at 1.0:\n<img width=\"391\" height=\"386\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79e12fc8-1bfa-4b2f-a4e6-761e1d7320db\" />\n\nI tested idle callback mode and physics callback mode and both work fine with drag set to 1, even at lower framerates.\n\nhere's an example of my FPS being at ~30-40 and with idle callback and drag set to 1.0:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a8f159ea-6a75-4dcd-8b8d-cc9ae770cdd1\n\nhere's the same setup but with drag at the default 0.4:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df42bf87-0e2d-4ff9-8341-1e8b02840453\n\nhuge difference.\n\nEDIT: after some more experimentation I believe this is a different issue all together having to do with the drag calculation, I'll open up my own issue for this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5510431152/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5510456173","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103229#issuecomment-5510456173","issue_url":"